% A Lightning offered HTLC (BOLT #3)
%
% The Logical English twin of a Bitcoin spending policy, written by the
% Miniscript translator. Who can spend the
% coin, when, and why: each rule is one spending path of the policy.
%
% Source: the Miniscript page
%         https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/
%
% The source, as written:
%     or(pk(key_revocation),and(pk(key_remote),or(pk(key_local),hash160(H))))
%
% The source, laid out (keys and hashes by their role, <like this>):
%     or(
%       pk(<the revocation key>),
%       and(
%         pk(<the remote node>),
%         or(pk(<the local node>),hash160(<the payment hash>))))
%
% The legend (role <- key or hash as written in the source):
%     the revocation key <- key_revocation
%     the remote node    <- key_remote
%     the local node     <- key_local
%     the payment hash   <- H
%
% What it says (the spending policy, by BIP 379's semantics):
%     any one of these:
%       a signature by the revocation key
%       all of these:
%         a signature by the remote node
%         any one of these:
%           a signature by the local node
%           the preimage of the payment hash (hash160)
%
% Try it in Minsc (the policy compiled to Miniscript, Script and an address,
% in the browser): the document "the policy in Minsc" below.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base bolt3_offered_htlc includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    the coin can be spent.
    the witness reveals the preimage of *a hash*; scenario element.
    the witness contains a signature by *a key*; scenario element.
    the hash function of *a hash* is *a function*.

the knowledge base bolt3_offered_htlc includes:

the Miniscript page is published at "https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/".
the text of the Miniscript page is at "sources/sipa_miniscript.txt".

the policy in Minsc is published at "https://min.sc/#c=//%20A%20Lightning%20offered%20HTLC%20(BOLT%20%233)%0A//%20The%20Logical%20English%20twin's%20policy%20(the%20Miniscript%20translator%20of%20Logical%20English).%0A$revocation_key%20=%20028071f961bf66967e8b92b2564cca5590e958305ce382ebeeb56e866b6baf3edc;%20%20%20//%20the%20revocation%20key%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A$remote_node%20=%20020df516861bd00658af8cf7c4655ceb20f61ba23075a37244dff7db5676c93234;%20%20%20//%20the%20remote%20node%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A$local_node%20=%20038fed93f74b169ba9410f1a39dde6b9c6eea84650dc79967a27f52757c197fbc8;%20%20%20//%20the%20local%20node%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A$payment_hash%20=%2005e3ba7e31a630b74c699bd5ddd19be207987f26;%20%20%20//%20the%20payment%20hash,%20hash160%20(the%20hash%20of%20a%20test%20preimage:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20hash)%0A%0Aor(pk($revocation_key),and(pk($remote_node),or(pk($local_node),hash160($payment_hash))))%0A".

the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is published at "https://tape.rewindbitcoin.com/explorer/address/bcrt1qm8sw9929w2rr3lch764hw3mzehxwlg7xeyd00xkey4l2k07zshzs0cdyq2".
the text of the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is at "sources/bolt3_offered_htlc.chain.json".

% The keys and hashes of the policy, as the source writes them.
the hash function of the payment hash is hash160.

% The spending paths of the policy.
rule revocation with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "The BOLT #3 offered HTLC policy: or(pk(key_revocation),and(pk(key_remote),or(pk(key_local),hash160(H))))":
the coin can be spent if
    the witness contains a signature by the revocation key.

rule remote_with_local_or_preimage with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "The BOLT #3 offered HTLC policy: or(pk(key_revocation),and(pk(key_remote),or(pk(key_local),hash160(H))))":
the coin can be spent if
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node
    and the witness contains a signature by the local node
        or the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.

scenario remote_with_local_or_preimage_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path remote_with_local_or_preimage_1 — the path needs: the preimage of the payment hash, a signature by the remote node
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario remote_with_local_or_preimage_1_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path remote_with_local_or_preimage_1 without requirement 1 — the path needs: the preimage of the payment hash, a signature by the remote node
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario remote_with_local_or_preimage_1_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path remote_with_local_or_preimage_1 without requirement 2 — the path needs: the preimage of the payment hash, a signature by the remote node
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario remote_with_local_or_preimage_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path remote_with_local_or_preimage_2 — the path needs: a signature by the local node, a signature by the remote node
    the witness contains a signature by the local node.
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario remote_with_local_or_preimage_2_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path remote_with_local_or_preimage_2 without requirement 1 — the path needs: a signature by the local node, a signature by the remote node
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario remote_with_local_or_preimage_2_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path remote_with_local_or_preimage_2 without requirement 2 — the path needs: a signature by the local node, a signature by the remote node
    the witness contains a signature by the local node.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario revocation is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path revocation — the path needs: a signature by the revocation key
    the witness contains a signature by the revocation key.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario revocation_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path revocation without requirement 1 — the path needs: a signature by the revocation key
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario no_witness is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % an empty witness
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario flip_now is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, no delay passed
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by the revocation key"]].

scenario flip_after_delays is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, every delay passed
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by the revocation key"]].

scenario lost_the_revocation_key is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the revocation key lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    the witness contains a signature by the local node.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness contains a signature by the remote node"]].

scenario lost_the_remote_node is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the remote node lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by the revocation key.
    the witness contains a signature by the local node.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness contains a signature by the revocation key"]].

scenario lost_the_local_node is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the local node lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by the revocation key.
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness contains a signature by the remote node", "remove: the witness contains a signature by the revocation key"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by the revocation key", "remove: the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash"]].

scenario chain_remote_with_local_or_preimage_1 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at transaction ee8f879ae37a7abee26fb39c2a3a602459dfbf8215e3b130b293012a31b7e755:
    % the chain accepted the spend: transaction ee8f879ae37a7abee26fb39c2a3a602459dfbf8215e3b130b293012a31b7e755
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario chain_remote_with_local_or_preimage_1_without_1 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_1_without_1:
    % the chain refused the spend: mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Script failed an OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY operation)
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment hash.
    spendable expects answers [].

