    % the chain refused the spend: mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Script failed an OP_EQUALVERIFY operation)
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario chain_remote_with_local_or_preimage_2 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at transaction d648dfa1acedd8592fe4eaf469cc0cbead5e4b8995055e24398a3b01fa86a57b:
    % the chain accepted the spend: transaction d648dfa1acedd8592fe4eaf469cc0cbead5e4b8995055e24398a3b01fa86a57b
    the witness contains a signature by the local node.
    the witness contains a signature by the remote node.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario chain_remote_with_local_or_preimage_2_without_2 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_2_without_2:
    % the chain refused the spend: mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Script failed an OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY operation)
    the witness contains a signature by the local node.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario chain_revocation is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at transaction e8c75778ecdf7e9a3c2c4b59000023966aa73b0196bc5162260f70bb0c870e11:
    % the chain accepted the spend: transaction e8c75778ecdf7e9a3c2c4b59000023966aa73b0196bc5162260f70bb0c870e11
    the witness contains a signature by the revocation key.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario chain_revocation_without_1 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_3_without_1:
    % the chain refused the spend: mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Operation not valid with the current stack size)
    spendable expects answers [].

query spendable is:
    the coin can be spent.

query flip_spend is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        the coin can be spent.

query flip_block is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        it is not the case that the coin can be spent.

query hash_functions is:
    the hash function of which hash is which function.

the view custody explainer is:
    the title is "Who can spend this coin: A Lightning offered HTLC (BOLT #3)".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the witness" are
        the witness reveals the preimage of a hash,
        the witness contains a signature by a key.
    the result is whether the coin can be spent.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped, as "What would let this coin be spent?".

